From f3ed99f71554f160bdb66479c007ee2ec3ccdfc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: work-ple <work-ple@flashnext.local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:02:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] [Model] Relocate ple_mmap to the platform-neutral
 common/ tree

VLLM_PLE_MMAP lives under vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/, so a ROCm build --
which imports the amd/ tree instead -- never imports the module, never
registers vllm::qwen4_exp_ple_mmap_forward, and silently treats
VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 as a no-op.

ple_mmap.py itself is platform-neutral: it makes no torch.cuda.* call, uses
no pinned memory, and its only platform touchpoint is
current_platform.dispatch_key, which RocmPlatform reports as "CUDA" exactly
like CudaPlatform. Move it next to common/ple.py so both trees can import it.

Pure relocation. No behavior change on the nvidia side:
  - git mv vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ple_mmap.py
           vllm/models/qwen4_exp/common/ple_mmap.py
  - nvidia/ple_layer.py, nvidia/model.py: 'from . import ple_mmap'
    -> 'from ..common import ple_mmap' (import blocks re-sorted)
  - tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_ple_mmap.py: the ple_mmap module import
    now points at common/ (nvidia.model stays nvidia.model)
  - vllm/envs.py: the VLLM_PLE_MMAP comment's file pointer follows the move

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D273pHHi5ExDmStQUAicb7
